SPRINT 3 RETROSPECTIVE

What went well:
• Financial screener engine was successfully implemented.
• Six screener presets were created and tested.
• Composite quality score was implemented.
• Peer percentile rankings were successfully generated for 11 peer groups.
• Radar charts were generated for peer analysis.
• screener_output.xlsx and peer_comparison.xlsx were successfully created.
• All automated tests passed successfully with 93 passed and 0 failures.

What could be improved:
• Duplicate company-year records were identified in the dataset.
• Some companies did not have an assigned peer group.
• Some SQL joins required database schema corrections.
• Excel report generation initially caused high memory usage.

What was learned:
• Learned how to implement financial screening and composite scoring.
• Learned how to calculate peer percentile rankings.
• Learned how to generate radar charts and Excel reports using Python.
• Improved understanding of SQLite, pandas, SQL joins, and automated testing.
• Learned how to debug and optimize data-processing code.

Action items for the next sprint:
• Improve data quality and handle duplicate records.
• Improve performance of large data-processing operations.
• Add more validation and automated tests.
• Improve visualization and reporting features.

Sprint status:
COMPLETED